  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This archive chronicle offers a genuinely original contribution to airlift historiography, most powerfully in its central thesis that paperwork functioned as an 'active governor' of the operation. The conceptual framing, particularly in chapters like 18 and 19, is strong, using archival poetics to make the ledgers and manifests feel alive. However, the book's structural discipline wanes in its final third, where the tight archival focus gives way to more generic strategic analysis and repetitive thesis restatements. Readers will value the core insight but may notice a drift in voice and specif",
